<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Stop timers; exit current valve state and treat valve state as "disabled"; clear any "lurking" commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENABLE-IN FALSE HANDLING
============================================================
If thsi instruction is on a false rung, or if EnableIn is false in FBD,
Total times, stroke counts and slow counts are maintained, but Current times are cleared.
The internal state is set to "Unknown".

Clear any "lurking" Commands.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(PCmd_ClearTotTimes) OTU(PCmd_ClearMaxTimes) OTU(PCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) OTU(PCmd_ClearSlowCounts) ,OTU(MCmd_ClearTotTimes) OTU(MCmd_ClearMaxTimes) OTU(MCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) OTU(MCmd_ClearSlowCounts) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The next five rungs cause the current state (whichever it is) to be exited.
This copies the previous state's "current" time to its "last" time
and resets the "current" time (and accumulated 10ths of hours, if applicable).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,1)[RES(Wrk_ClosedT) ,MOV(Val_CurrClosedT,Wrk_LastClosedT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrClosedTenths) ,CLR(Val_CurrClosedT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,2)[RES(Wrk_OpeningT) ,MOV(Val_CurrOpeningT,Wrk_LastOpeningT) ,CLR(Val_CurrOpeningT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,3)[RES(Wrk_OpenedT) ,MOV(Val_CurrOpenedT,Wrk_LastOpenedT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrOpenedTenths) ,CLR(Val_CurrOpenedT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,4)[RES(Wrk_ClosingT) ,MOV(Val_CurrClosingT,Wrk_LastClosingT) ,CLR(Val_CurrClosingT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,5)[RES(Wrk_StopOtherT) ,MOV(Val_CurrStopOtherT,Wrk_LastStopotherT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrStopOtherTenths) ,CLR(Val_CurrStopOtherT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The internal state is set to "unknown" (disabled).
When normal execution (Logic routine) is resumed, when an input shows the valve
in a known condition, a transition to the corresponding state will occur.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung scans all the retentive timers FALSE to stop them.

NOTE the NEQ of Wrk_State, which was cleared on the rung above.
THIS RUNG IS ALWAYS FALSE AND MUST BE SCANNED THAT WAY FOR PROPER OPERATION.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Wrk_State,0)[RTO(Wrk_ClosedT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotClosedT,?,?) ,RTO(Wrk_OpeningT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotOpeningT,?,?) ,RTO(Wrk_OpenedT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotOpenedT,?,?) ,RTO(Wrk_ClosingT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotClosingT,?,?) ,RTO(Wrk_StopOtherT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotStopOtherT,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Accumulate Valve open/close stroke count and time statistics]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_ValveStats:  PROCESS -- 2-STATE VALVE STATISTICS
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib.
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Unmodified for Library of Process Objects 3.1, up-rev only.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
This Instruction monitors the "Closed" and "Opened" Status of a 2-state valve
device (and, optionally, a "Stopped" or other status), and provides:
TIMES:
* Current time traveling Open (current opening)
* Stroke time for last successful Open stroke (last opening)
* Total time traveling Open (total opening)
* Maximum time travelling Open (maximum opening)
* Moving average Open Stroke time (last 10 successful strokes)
* Current time traveling Closed (current closing)
* Stroke time for last successful Close stroke (last closing)
* Total time traveling Closed (total closing)
* Maximum time travelling Closed (maximum closing)
* Moving average Close Stroke time (last 10 successful strokes)
* Current time in Open position (current opened)
* Previous time in Open position (last opened)
* Total time in Open position (total opened)
* Maximum time in Open position (maximum opened)
* Current time in Closed position (current closed)
* Previous time in Closed position (last closed)
* Total time in Closed position (total closed)
* Maximum time in Closed position (maximum closed)
and, if option enabled
* Current time in Stopped / Other position (current stopped)
* Previous time in Stopped / Other position (last stopped)
* Total time in Stopped / Other position (total stopped)
* Maximum time in Stopped / Other position (maximum stopped)
COUNTS:
* Count of complete Open strokes (from Closed to Opened)
* Count of complete Close strokes (from Opened to Closed)
* Count of incomplete Open strokes (from Closed to Moving back to Closed)
* Count of incomplete Close strokes (from Opened to Moving back to Opened)
* Count of Slow Opens (time to open greater than configured threshold)
* Count of Slow Closes (time to close greater than configured threshold)
and, if option enabled
* Count of times in Stopped / Other position
RESETS:
* Commands to allow clearing of the Total Times, clearing of the Maximum Times,
clearing of the Stroke Counts and clearing of the Slow Counts
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)CONCAT(Cfg_StopOtherDesc,Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs handle received Commands.  This object has no Modes and
Commands are accepted regardless of Mode.  Commands should be
restriceted to authorized personnel (typically at a maintenance level).

PCmd_ClearTotTimes: Program Command to Clear various Total Time statistics
MCmd_ClearTotTimes: Maintenance Command to Clear various Total Time statistics]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)[XIC(PCmd_ClearTotTimes) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ClearTotTimes) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(MCmd_ClearTotTimes) OTU(MCmd_ClearTotTimes) ][RES(Wrk_TotClosedT) CLR(Wrk_TotClosedTenths) RES(Wrk_TotClosingT) CLR(Wrk_TotClosingTenths) ,RES(Wrk_TotOpenedT) CLR(Wrk_TotOpenedTenths) RES(Wrk_TotOpeningT) CLR(Wrk_TotOpeningTenths) ,RES(Wrk_TotStopOtherT) CLR(Wrk_TotStopOtherTenths) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PCmd_ClearMaxTimes: Program Command to Clear various Maximum Time statistics
MCmd_ClearMaxTimes: Maintenance Command to Clear various Maximum Time statistics]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_ClearMaxTimes) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ClearMaxTimes) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(MCmd_ClearMaxTimes) OTU(MCmd_ClearMaxTimes) ][CLR(Wrk_MaxClosedT) CLR(Wrk_MaxOpeningT) ,CLR(Wrk_MaxOpenedT) CLR(Wrk_MaxClosingT) ,CLR(Wrk_MaxStopOtherT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PCmd_ClearMAvgs: Program Command to Clear the Moving Averages for Open and Close stroke times
MCmd_ClearMAvgs: Maintenance Command to Clear the Moving Averages for Open and Close stroke times]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_ClearMAvgs) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ClearMAvgs) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(MCmd_ClearMAvgs) OTU(MCmd_ClearMAvgs) ]CLR(Wrk_MAvgOpenC)CLR(Wrk_MAvgCloseC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PCmd_ClearStrokeCounts: Program Command to Clear Count of Open and Close Strokes (complete and incomplete)
MCmd_ClearStrokeCounts: Maintenance Command to Clear Count Open and Close Strokes]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(MCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) OTU(MCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) ][CLR(Wrk_CpltCloseC) ,CLR(Wrk_CpltOpenC) ,CLR(Wrk_IncpltCloseC) ,CLR(Wrk_IncpltOpenC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PCmd_ClearSlowCounts: Program Command to Clear Valve Slow Open and Slow Close Counts
MCmd_ClearStrokeCounts: Maintenance Command to Clear Valve Slow Open and Slow Close Counts]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_ClearSlowCounts) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ClearSlowCounts) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(MCmd_ClearSlowCounts) OTU(MCmd_ClearSlowCounts) ][CLR(Wrk_SlowOpenC) ,CLR(Wrk_SlowCloseC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
This rung checks the Slow Open Time and Slow Close Time Configuration values.
If either is negative or larger than (max time accumulator time minus one second),
show that there is an Invalid Configuration (faceplate breadcrumb: magenta "X").]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LIM(2147482.0,Cfg_SlowOpenT,-1.40129846E-45) ,LIM(2147482.0,Cfg_SlowCloseT,-1.40129846E-45) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ACCUMULATE TIMES BASED ON VALVE STATE
============================================================
The rungs that follow accumulate Time Currently In State and Total Time in State
for each of the valve's various states and check if the current time is larger
than the recorded maximum (recording a new maximum if so).

The Total times and the sustained state (Closed, Opened, Stopped) 
Current times use a "10ths of hours" accumulator to allow a total
time larger than a timer accumulator will allow (about 24 days).

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
CLOSED State Timers
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Record the Current and Total time the valve is Closed,
and the maximum time ever spent in the Closed state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,1)[RTO(Wrk_ClosedT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotClosedT,?,?) ,GRT(Wrk_ClosedT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_CurrClosedTenths,1,Wrk_CurrClosedTenths) SUB(Wrk_ClosedT.ACC,360000,Wrk_ClosedT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_CurrClosedT,Wrk_CurrClosedTenths*360.0+Wrk_ClosedT.ACC/1000.0) ,GRT(Val_CurrClosedT,Wrk_MaxClosedT) MOV(Val_CurrClosedT,Wrk_MaxClosedT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The total time must be calculated independent of state, in cas a ClearTotTimes command is received.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_TotClosedT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_TotClosedTenths,1,Wrk_TotClosedTenths) SUB(Wrk_TotClosedT.ACC,360000,Wrk_TotClosedT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_TotClosedT,Wrk_TotClosedTenths/10.0+Wrk_TotClosedT.ACC/3600000.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
OPENING (travelling open) State Timers
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Record the Current and Total time the valve is Opening,
and the maximum time ever spent in the Opening state.

Note: the 10ths accumulator is not used for the Current
Opening Time.  The valve should take less than 24 days to open!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,2)[RTO(Wrk_OpeningT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotOpeningT,?,?) ,OTU(Wrk_SlowOpenSts) ,DIV(Wrk_OpeningT.ACC,1000.0,Val_CurrOpeningT) ,GRT(Val_CurrOpeningT,Wrk_MaxOpeningT) MOV(Val_CurrOpeningT,Wrk_MaxOpeningT) ,GRT(Val_CurrOpeningT,Cfg_SlowOpenT) [OTL(Wrk_SlowOpenSts) ,ONS(Wrk_SlowOpenONS) ADD(Wrk_SlowOpenC,1,Wrk_SlowOpenC) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The total time must be calculated independent of state, in cas a ClearTotTimes command is received.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_TotOpeningT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_TotOpeningTenths,1,Wrk_TotOpeningTenths) SUB(Wrk_TotOpeningT.ACC,360000,Wrk_TotOpeningT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_TotOpeningT,Wrk_TotOpeningTenths/10.0+Wrk_TotOpeningT.ACC/3600000.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
OPENED State Timers
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Record the Current and Total time the valve is Opened,
and the maximum time ever spent in the Opened state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,3)[RTO(Wrk_OpenedT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotOpenedT,?,?) ,GRT(Wrk_OpenedT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_CurrOpenedTenths,1,Wrk_CurrOpenedTenths) SUB(Wrk_OpenedT.ACC,360000,Wrk_OpenedT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_CurrOpenedT,Wrk_CurrOpenedTenths*360.0+Wrk_OpenedT.ACC/1000.0) ,GRT(Val_CurrOpenedT,Wrk_MaxOpenedT) MOV(Val_CurrOpenedT,Wrk_MaxOpenedT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The total time must be calculated independent of state, in cas a ClearTotTimes command is received.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_TotOpenedT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_TotOpenedTenths,1,Wrk_TotOpenedTenths) SUB(Wrk_TotOpenedT.ACC,360000,Wrk_TotOpenedT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_TotOpenedT,Wrk_TotOpenedTenths/10.0+Wrk_TotOpenedT.ACC/3600000.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
CLOSING (travelling closed) State Timers
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Record the Current and Total time the valve is Closing,
and the maximum time ever spent in the Closing state.

Note: the 10ths accumulator is not used for the Current
Closing Time.  The valve should take less than 24 days to close!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,4)[RTO(Wrk_ClosingT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotClosingT,?,?) ,OTU(Wrk_SlowCloseSts) ,DIV(Wrk_ClosingT.ACC,1000.0,Val_CurrClosingT) ,GRT(Val_CurrClosingT,Wrk_MaxClosingT) MOV(Val_CurrClosingT,Wrk_MaxClosingT) ,GRT(Val_CurrClosingT,Cfg_SlowCloseT) [OTL(Wrk_SlowCloseSts) ,ONS(Wrk_SlowCloseONS) ADD(Wrk_SlowCloseC,1,Wrk_SlowCloseC) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The total time must be calculated independent of state, in cas a ClearTotTimes command is received.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_TotClosingT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_TotClosingTenths,1,Wrk_TotClosingTenths) SUB(Wrk_TotClosingT.ACC,360000,Wrk_TotClosingT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_TotClosingT,Wrk_TotClosingTenths/10.0+Wrk_TotClosingT.ACC/3600000.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STOPPED / OTHER State Timers
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Record the Current and Total time the valve is Stopped (or in Other position),
and the maximum time ever spent in the Stopped / Other state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,5)[RTO(Wrk_StopOtherT,?,?) RTO(Wrk_TotStopOtherT,?,?) ,OTU(Wrk_SlowCloseSts) OTU(Wrk_SlowOpenSts) ,GRT(Wrk_StopOtherT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_CurrStopOtherTenths,1,Wrk_CurrStopOtherTenths) SUB(Wrk_StopOtherT.ACC,360000,Wrk_StopOtherT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_CurrStopOtherT,Wrk_CurrStopOtherTenths*360.0+Wrk_StopOtherT.ACC/1000.0) ,GRT(Val_CurrStopOtherT,Wrk_MaxStopOtherT) MOV(Val_CurrStopOtherT,Wrk_MaxStopOtherT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The total time must be calculated independent of state, in cas a ClearTotTimes command is received.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Wrk_TotStopOtherT.ACC,360000) ADD(Wrk_TotStopOtherTenths,1,Wrk_TotStopOtherTenths) SUB(Wrk_TotStopOtherT.ACC,360000,Wrk_TotStopOtherT.ACC) ,CPT(Val_TotStopOtherT,Wrk_TotStopOtherTenths/10.0+Wrk_TotStopOtherT.ACC/3600000.0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE STATE TRANSITIONS
============================================================
The rungs that follow check for input changes to transition out of the current state
into a new state.
Valid transitions are shown in the State Diagram in the SMDS and Reference Manual.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
UNKNOWN / POWERUP STATE
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If the valve state is Powerup (State 0) or Unknown (invalid, outside
the range 1 to 5), transition to:
* Closed, if the Closed position is confirmed
* Opened, if the Opened position is confirmed
* Stopped / Other, if that position is confirmed. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIM(6,Wrk_State,0)[XIC(Inp_Closed) MOV(1,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Inp_Opened) MOV(3,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Inp_StopOther) MOV(5,Wrk_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
CLOSED State
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If the valve state is Closed (1), transition to:
* Opening, if the Closed position is no longer confirmed
* Stopped / Other, if that position is confirmed. 

Upon exiting the Closed state, copy the Current Closed time to the
Last Closed time and reset the Current Closed time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,1)[XIO(Inp_Closed) MOV(2,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStopOther) XIC(Inp_StopOther) ADD(Wrk_StopOtherC,1,Wrk_StopOtherC) MOV(5,Wrk_State) ][RES(Wrk_ClosedT) ,MOV(Val_CurrClosedT,Wrk_LastClosedT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrClosedTenths) ,CLR(Val_CurrClosedT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
OPENING State
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If the valve state is Opening (2), transition to:
* Opened, if the Opened position is confirmed (and count a Complete Open Stroke)
* Closed, if the Closed position is  confirmed (and count an Incomplete Open Stroke)
* Stopped / Other, if that position is confirmed (and count a Stopped/Other occurrence
AND an Incomplete Open Stroke!)

Upon exiting the Opening state, copy the Current Opening time to the
Last Opening time and reset the Current Opening time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,2)[XIC(Inp_Opened) OTE(Wrk_MAvgOpenONS) ADD(Wrk_CpltOpenC,1,Wrk_CpltOpenC) MOV(3,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Inp_Closed) ADD(Wrk_IncpltOpenC,1,Wrk_IncpltOpenC) MOV(1,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStopOther) XIC(Inp_StopOther) ADD(Wrk_StopOtherC,1,Wrk_StopOtherC) ADD(Wrk_IncpltOpenC,1,Wrk_IncpltOpenC) MOV(5,Wrk_State) ][RES(Wrk_OpeningT) ,MOV(Val_CurrOpeningT,Wrk_LastOpeningT) ,CLR(Val_CurrOpeningT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
OEPNED State
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If the valve state is Opened (3), transition to:
* Closing, if the Opened position is no longer confirmed
* Stopped / Other, if that position is confirmed. 

Upon exiting the Opened state, copy the Current Opened time to the
Last Opened time and reset the Current Opened time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,3)[XIO(Inp_Opened) MOV(4,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStopOther) XIC(Inp_StopOther) ADD(Wrk_StopOtherC,1,Wrk_StopOtherC) MOV(5,Wrk_State) ][RES(Wrk_OpenedT) ,MOV(Val_CurrOpenedT,Wrk_LastOpenedT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrOpenedTenths) ,CLR(Val_CurrOpenedT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
CLOSING State
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If the valve state is Closing (4), transition to:
* Closed, if the Closed position is  confirmed (and count a Complete Close Stroke)
* Opened, if the Opened position is confirmed (and count an Incomplete Close Stroke)
* Stopped / Other, if that position is confirmed (and count a Stopped/Other occurrence
AND an Incomplete Close Stroke!)

Upon exiting the Opening state, copy the Current Opening time to the
Last Opening time and reset the Current Opening time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,4)[XIC(Inp_Closed) OTE(Wrk_MAvgCloseONS) ADD(Wrk_CpltCloseC,1,Wrk_CpltCloseC) MOV(1,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Inp_Opened) ADD(Wrk_IncpltCloseC,1,Wrk_IncpltCloseC) MOV(3,Wrk_State) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStopOther) XIC(Inp_StopOther) ADD(Wrk_StopOtherC,1,Wrk_StopOtherC) ADD(Wrk_IncpltCloseC,1,Wrk_IncpltCloseC) MOV(5,Wrk_State) ][RES(Wrk_ClosingT) ,MOV(Val_CurrClosingT,Wrk_LastClosingT) ,CLR(Val_CurrClosingT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STOPPED State
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If the valve state is Stopped (5), transition to:
* Closed, if the Stopped position is no longer confirmed AND the Closed position IS confirmed
* Opened, if the Stopped position is no longer confirmed AND the Opened position IS confirmed

Upon exiting the Stopped state, copy the Current Stopped time to the
Last Stopped time and reset the Current Stopped time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,5)[[XIO(Inp_StopOther) ,XIO(Cfg_HasStopOther) ] XIC(Inp_Closed) MOV(1,Wrk_State) ,[XIO(Inp_StopOther) ,XIO(Cfg_HasStopOther) ] XIC(Inp_Opened) MOV(3,Wrk_State) ][RES(Wrk_StopOtherT) ,MOV(Val_CurrStopOtherT,Wrk_LastStopotherT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrStopOtherTenths) ,CLR(Val_CurrStopOtherT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CALCULATE MOVING AVERAGES OF STROKE TIMES
============================================================
The rungs that follow accumulate the stroke times for the last 10 successful strokes
(each way, 10 open strokes, 10 clese strokes) and return the Moving Average
Stroke Time for each direction.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Open Stroke Time Moving Average
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
First, let's make sure we don't fault the processor with a bad array index.
If the stroke time sample count is invalid, force it to be in range (valid = 0 to 10).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Wrk_MAvgOpenC,0) CLR(Wrk_MAvgOpenC) ,GRT(Wrk_MAvgOpenC,10) MOV(10,Wrk_MAvgOpenC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the count of items in the sample array is zero, the moving average
was cleared (by command).
Return a ZERO to the moving average Value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_MAvgOpenC,0)CLR(Val_MAvgOpeningT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a successful Open stroke occured, record the data in the
 moving average sample array.
If there are already 10 items in the array, shift the data up and
 add this new time at the end.
If there are NOT already 10 items in the array, put this stroke time
in the next available array position.
Now the count of items in the sample array is 1 to 10 (usually 10), so return the average of that number
of samples in the reported moving average stroke time Value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_MAvgOpenONS)[EQU(Wrk_MAvgOpenC,10) COP(Wrk_MAvgOpenSamp[1],Wrk_MAvgOpenSamp[0],9) MOV(Wrk_LastOpeningT,Wrk_MAvgOpenSamp[9]) ,LIM(0,Wrk_MAvgOpenC,9) MOV(Wrk_LastOpeningT,Wrk_MAvgOpenSamp[Wrk_MAvgOpenC]) ADD(Wrk_MAvgOpenC,1,Wrk_MAvgOpenC) ,RES(Wrk_MAvgAveOpen) MOV(Wrk_MAvgOpenC,Wrk_MAvgAveOpen.LEN) AVE(Wrk_MAvgOpenSamp,0,Val_MAvgOpeningT,Wrk_MAvgAveOpen,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Close Stroke Time Moving Average
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
First, let's make sure we don't fault the processor with a bad array index.
If the stroke time sample count is invalid, force it to be in range (valid = 0 to 10).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Wrk_MAvgCloseC,0) CLR(Wrk_MAvgCloseC) ,GRT(Wrk_MAvgCloseC,10) MOV(10,Wrk_MAvgCloseC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the count of items in the sample array is zero, the moving average
was cleared (by command).
Return a ZERO to the moving average Value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_MAvgCloseC,0)CLR(Val_MAvgClosingT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a successful Close stroke occured, record the data in the
 moving average sample array.
If there are already 10 items in the array, shift the data up and
 add this new time at the end.
If there are NOT already 10 items in the array, put this stroke time
in the next available array position.
Now the count of items in the sample array is 1 to 10 (usually 10), so return the average of that number
of samples in the reported moving average stroke time Value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_MAvgCloseONS)[EQU(Wrk_MAvgCloseC,10) COP(Wrk_MAvgCloseSamp[1],Wrk_MAvgCloseSamp[0],9) MOV(Wrk_LastClosingT,Wrk_MAvgCloseSamp[9]) ,LIM(0,Wrk_MAvgCloseC,9) MOV(Wrk_LastClosingT,Wrk_MAvgCloseSamp[Wrk_MAvgCloseC]) ADD(Wrk_MAvgCloseC,1,Wrk_MAvgCloseC) ,RES(Wrk_MAvgAveClose) MOV(Wrk_MAvgCloseC,Wrk_MAvgAveClose.LEN) AVE(Wrk_MAvgCloseSamp[0],0,Val_MAvgClosingT,Wrk_MAvgAveClose,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PUBLISH VALUES AND STATUS
============================================================
The rungs that follow move internal working values and status (which use
Work registers to make them "not visible", avoiding unintentional overwrites)
to public Values and Status.
(Some Values are calculated directly, in logic above.)

This rung publishes the Stroke Counts. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_CpltOpenC,Val_CpltOpenC)MOV(Wrk_CpltCloseC,Val_CpltCloseC)MOV(Wrk_IncpltOpenC,Val_IncpltOpenC)MOV(Wrk_IncpltCloseC,Val_IncpltCloseC)MOV(Wrk_StopOtherC,Val_StopOtherC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung publishes the Slow Valve Counts.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_SlowOpenC,Val_SlowOpenC)MOV(Wrk_SlowCloseC,Val_SlowCloseC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung publishes the "Last" position time statistics.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_LastClosedT,Val_LastClosedT)MOV(Wrk_LastClosingT,Val_LastClosingT)MOV(Wrk_LastOpenedT,Val_LastOpenedT)MOV(Wrk_LastOpeningT,Val_LastOpeningT)MOV(Wrk_LastStopotherT,Val_LastStopOtherT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung publishes the "Maximum" position time statistics.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DIV(Wrk_MaxClosedT,3600.0,Val_MaxClosedT)MOV(Wrk_MaxOpeningT,Val_MaxOpeningT)DIV(Wrk_MaxOpenedT,3600.0,Val_MaxOpenedT)MOV(Wrk_MaxClosingT,Val_MaxClosingT)DIV(Wrk_MaxStopOtherT,3600.0,Val_MaxStopOtherT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies the internal status bits to public Status.

(NOTE:  These are copeid rather than aliased because the Wrk bits are
only written as needed.  Buffering keeps writes to
Sts_SlowCloseSts and Sts_SlowCloseSts from
affecting the internal state of the instruction instance.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_SlowCloseSts) OTE(Sts_SlowClose) ,XIC(Wrk_SlowOpenSts) OTE(Sts_SlowOpen) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear current times, treat valve state as "unknown" and clear any "lurking" commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
POWERUP / PRESCAN HANDLING
============================================================
Total times, stroke counts and slow counts are maintained
through a power cycle.  Current times are cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[RES(Wrk_ClosedT) RES(Wrk_OpeningT) RES(Wrk_OpenedT) RES(Wrk_ClosingT) RES(Wrk_StopOtherT) ,CLR(Wrk_CurrClosedTenths) CLR(Wrk_CurrOpenedTenths) CLR(Wrk_CurrStopOtherTenths) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The internal state is set to "unknown".  When an input shows the valve
in a known condition, the main logic will transition to the corresponding state]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear any "lurking" Commands.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(PCmd_ClearTotTimes) OTU(PCmd_ClearMaxTimes) OTU(PCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) OTU(PCmd_ClearSlowCounts) ,OTU(MCmd_ClearTotTimes) OTU(MCmd_ClearMaxTimes) OTU(MCmd_ClearStrokeCounts) OTU(MCmd_ClearSlowCounts) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
